# The loop over the names of a layout walks the list that Object.keys made. Each turn loads a name and asks one pure function which of the names of the layout it is.
# LOOP-LABEL: steps by 1
# LOOP-LABEL: steps by 1
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[key]] = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:indexedContiguousProperties, {{*}}:GetArrayElement)
# LOOP: Int64 b@[[which]] = Patchpoint(b@[[key]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), pureFunction = {{*}}(children), ControlDependent, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# The answer is compared with one name after the other, and each arm is one load of a double from its slot: no lookup by name.
# LOOP-NEXT: Int32 b@[[isFirst]] = Equal(b@[[which]], ${{*}}, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# LOOP-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isFirst]], Terminal, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# LOOP: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[point]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# LOOP: Double b@{{*}} = Add(b@{{*}}, b@{{*}}, {{*}}:Add)
# LOOP: Int32 b@{{*}} = Equal(b@[[which]], ${{*}}, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# LOOP: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[point]], offset = 24, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# LOOP: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[point]], offset = 32, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# LOOP-LABEL: end of loop
# Nothing in this loop but its poll can throw or allocate, and the length of the list is not loaded again. Beside a call a poll costs little, so it stays in the turn.
# CALLS-LABEL: steps by 1
# CALLS-LABEL: steps by 1
# CALLS-NOT: Reads:Butterfly_publicLength
# CALLS-NOT: Reads:JSObject_butterfly
# CALLS-COUNT-1: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-NOT: Reads:Butterfly_publicLength
# CALLS-NOT: Reads:JSObject_butterfly
# CALLS-LABEL: end of loop
# The counts hold a call, whose moves follow the calling convention: not for Windows.
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 12, patchpoints: 3, {{*}} steps by 1
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 12, patchpoints: 3, {{*}} steps by 1
